{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0001", "block": 1, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 84, "sha256": "288681fae453fe4d", "text": "Table 5. Example attacker inputs to gain unauthorized access to an internal network."}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0002", "block": 2, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 46, "sha256": "a432b7025a623974", "text": "Sensitive Data Exfiltration via Mounted Volume"}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0003", "block": 3, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 13, "sha256": "808c44a3b095245b", "text": "**Objective**"}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0004", "block": 4, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 472, "sha256": "29607fe5e02f4ca7", "text": "The attacker abuses the code interpreter tool used by the stock agent to access credential files that may be mistakenly mounted into the container. To enable file exchange between the agent and the code interpreter, it is common to mount a directory from the host into the container. However, if this mounted volume includes sensitive data --- such as credentials, source code or configuration files --- the attacker can exploit the interpreter to exfiltrate these assets."}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0005", "block": 5, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 777, "sha256": "8d92ac93d93d5784", "text": "As illustrated in Figure 7, the attacker sends a malicious payload to the stock agent's code interpreter. This payload executes code within the container to locate and extract sensitive files from the mounted directory. ![Illustration depicting a threat actor using prompt injection in agentic AI. The process includes the Orchestration Agent, Prompt Injection, Code Interpreter, and Stock Agent, connected by lines indicating communication paths, all centralized around the Host. A Key File is shown connected to the network. The Code Interpreter goes through Docker before connecting to the key file.](https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/word-image-166518-140037-7.png) Figure 7. Abuse code interpreter to steal credential files stored on the host."}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0006", "block": 6, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 26, "sha256": "7b4c21891e66fe51", "text": "Attack Payload Explanation"}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0007", "block": 7, "kind": "para", "translate": true, "chars": 609, "sha256": "06b4768c478cdf1d", "text": "The example attacker inputs in Table 6 direct the agent to search for files in a mounted volume for credentials. Note that the attacker inputs refer to the stock agent as a Portfolio Management Agent. The path of the mounted directory is often explicitly specified in the tool's description or in the agent's instructions, allowing the agent to read and write files during normal operations. The payload also instructs the agent to Base-64 encode the output because most frontier LLMs have internal safeguards that prevent generating responses containing sensitive information such as secrets and credentials."}
{"slug": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5", "id": "unit42-paloaltonetworks-com-agentic-ai-threats__p5#b0008", "block": 8, "kind": "heading", "translate": true, "chars": 23, "sha256": "b0a00415e1584a68", "text": "Putting It All Together"}
